# Upload exclusion list for `gcloud run deploy --source` (T-02-11).
#
# gcloud generates a Git-compatible ignore list ONLY while this file is absent.
# The moment it exists it takes over completely, so it must re-state everything
# .gitignore covers that must not reach a Cloud Storage build bucket. The repo
# root holds ~490 MB of gitignored personal health exports plus a local
# virtualenv; uploading them would copy medical data into a build artifact store.
#
# It deliberately does NOT exclude backend/, pyproject.toml, uv.lock,
# .python-version or Procfile - all five must reach the builder.
.git/
.gitignore
.gcloudignore
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.DS_Store
.claude/
.planning/
# Local environment files. A build must never carry a developer .env.
.env
.env.*
# Personal health-data exports and scratch docs.
export.xml
export_cda.xml
records.csv
workouts.csv
activity_summary.csv
BRETT blueprint.md
